M2-c145 L10 M1 | card: Is differentiability of F on (a, b) enough for the integral formula, w | item: “Differentiability of \(F\) on \((a, b)\) is enough; nothing is needed about \(F'\).”
M2-c146 L10 M2 | card: Is the integral from a to x of f equal to F(x), with no constant to su | item: “The integral \(\int_a^x f\) equals \(F(x)\), with no constant to subtract.”
M2-c147 L10 M3 | card: Does the fundamental theorem apply only to polynomials? | item: “The fundamental theorem applies only to polynomials.”
M2-c161 L11 M1 | card: Is the boundary term of integration by parts always zero? | item: “In integration by parts the boundary term always vanishes.”
M2-c162 L11 M2 | card: Does substitution leave the limits of integration unchanged? | item: “Substitution does not change the limits of integration.”
M2-c163 L11 M3 | card: Does integration by parts apply to any two differentiable functions? | item: “Integration by parts applies to any two differentiable functions.”
M2-c176 L12 M2 | card: Does 1/x tending to 0 at infinity guarantee convergence of the integra | item: “If \(f(x) \to 0\) as \(x \to \infty\), then \(\int_1^\infty f\) converges.”
M2-c177 L12 M1 | card: Does a large enough truncation give the exact improper value? | item: “A large enough truncation gives the exact improper value.”
